{
  "sn35.244:0.1": "Linked Discourses 35.244 ",
  "sn35.244:0.2": "19. The Simile of the Vipers ",
  "sn35.244:0.3": "Entailing Suffering ",
  "sn35.244:1.1": "“Mendicants, when a mendicant truly understands the origin and disappearance of all things that entail suffering, ",
  "sn35.244:1.2": "then they’ve seen sensual pleasures in such a way that they have no underlying tendency for desire, affection, infatuation, and passion for sensual pleasures. ",
  "sn35.244:1.3": "And they’ve awakened to a way of conduct and a way of living such that, when they live in that way, bad, unskillful qualities of covetousness and displeasure don’t overwhelm them. ",
  "sn35.244:2.1": "And how does a mendicant truly understand the origin and disappearance of all things that entail suffering? ",
  "sn35.244:2.2": "‘Such is form, such is the origin of form, such is the disappearance of form. ",
  "sn35.244:2.3": "Such is feeling … ",
  "sn35.244:2.4": "perception … ",
  "sn35.244:2.5": "choices … ",
  "sn35.244:2.6": "consciousness, such is the origin of consciousness, such is the disappearance of consciousness.’ ",
  "sn35.244:2.7": "That’s how a mendicant truly understands the origin and disappearance of all things that entail suffering. ",
  "sn35.244:3.1": "And how has a mendicant seen sensual pleasures in such a way that they have no underlying tendency for desire, affection, infatuation, and passion for sensual pleasures? ",
